1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,212
Nintendo Switch Sports shows a win banner and
a celebration after a match.

2
00:00:05,212 --> 00:00:09,882
Ring Fit Adventure accompanies exercise
movements with evaluation feedback.

3
00:00:09,882 --> 00:00:14,622
The same score can feel different when a game
acknowledges what you did.

4
00:00:14,622 --> 00:00:18,822
We can distinguish calculating success from
expressing recognition of that success.

5
00:00:18,822 --> 00:00:24,292
Today we examine how to recognize an action,
rather than how to add rewards.

6
00:00:24,292 --> 00:00:28,862
Our original defense test applies the same
inputs and collision rules to both screens.

7
00:00:28,862 --> 00:00:31,182
We change the timing, wording, strength, and
position of the praise.

8
00:00:31,182 --> 00:00:37,280
Enjoyment needs human testing, while logs can
verify exactly what changed.

9
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,492
First, compare when the praise appears.

10
00:00:40,492 --> 00:00:43,782
Both characters block the same attack at the
same moment.

11
00:00:43,782 --> 00:00:47,802
One side responds promptly; the other responds
much later.

12
00:00:47,802 --> 00:00:52,552
If the next attack arrives during the wait, it
is harder to connect praise with the action.

13
00:00:52,552 --> 00:00:56,312
Try attaching a brief response close to the
successful collision result.

14
00:00:56,312 --> 00:01:00,882
The signal can acknowledge the recent action
without a large display.

15
00:01:00,882 --> 00:01:04,402
This does not prescribe one delay for every
game.

16
00:01:04,402 --> 00:01:08,800
It is a reason to check overlap with the next
action at normal speed.

17
00:01:09,520 --> 00:01:13,762
A generic compliment may not explain what went
well.

18
00:01:13,762 --> 00:01:17,692
This test blocks an attack, then moves upward
to dodge the next one.

19
00:01:17,692 --> 00:01:22,812
One screen repeats the same praise; the other
distinguishes blocking from dodging.

20
00:01:22,812 --> 00:01:26,062
A brief label names the action actually
verified by the collision rules.

21
00:01:26,062 --> 00:01:31,112
Calling a button press a perfect block can
misrepresent the result.

22
00:01:31,112 --> 00:01:35,202
Choose the label from the successful outcome,
rather than the input event alone.

23
00:01:35,202 --> 00:01:39,522
That information can help the player identify
an action to try again.

24
00:01:39,522 --> 00:01:44,000
Praise need not become an instruction manual,
but it need not hide its reason.

25
00:01:44,720 --> 00:01:49,052
Using the largest celebration for every
success removes a distinction between moments.

26
00:01:49,052 --> 00:01:54,412
A match win in Switch Sports illustrates a
broader celebration at a stopping point.

27
00:01:54,412 --> 00:01:59,232
The same scale after every small success can
cover the next situation.

28
00:01:59,232 --> 00:02:02,652
Our test uses a small marker for a single
block.

29
00:02:02,652 --> 00:02:06,652
A stronger response appears only when a
sequence of successful blocks is verified.

30
00:02:06,652 --> 00:02:11,832
The score and successful-action count stay
equal; only presentation strength changes.

31
00:02:11,832 --> 00:02:14,862
Distinguish an individual success, a sequence,
and the completion of a longer section.

32
00:02:14,862 --> 00:02:19,040
This aligns the scale of the recognition with
the actual accomplishment.

33
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:24,232
Unconditionally calling a failure perfect can
undermine trust in the praise.

34
00:02:24,232 --> 00:02:28,662
Both screens receive the same inputs,
deliberately missing one attack.

35
00:02:28,662 --> 00:02:32,972
Health falls equally, but one side still
claims the performance was perfect.

36
00:02:32,972 --> 00:02:37,042
The other side shows the hit and acknowledges
only the blocks that actually succeeded.

37
00:02:37,042 --> 00:02:41,752
We can name a genuine partial success without
hiding the failure.

38
00:02:41,752 --> 00:02:44,502
Every failure does not need a compliment.

39
00:02:44,502 --> 00:02:48,882
Show a retry clue separately, and distinguish
signals for success and failure.

40
00:02:48,882 --> 00:02:53,440
Supportive wording should remain connected to
actual outcomes to inform another attempt.

41
00:02:54,160 --> 00:02:58,382
Finally, check whether the praise obstructs
the next action.

42
00:02:58,382 --> 00:03:03,342
Large text placed over the attack can cover
the area where the next threat must be read.

43
00:03:03,342 --> 00:03:07,752
This comparison preserves outcomes and wording
while changing position and area.

44
00:03:07,752 --> 00:03:11,822
Compare a small marker near the action with a
brief response near the edge.

45
00:03:11,822 --> 00:03:14,452
Check that neither moving targets nor
necessary

46
00:03:14,452 --> 00:03:16,632
information are obscured at phone size.

47
00:03:16,632 --> 00:03:21,792
Record what is recognized, when it is
recognized, and how strongly it is expressed.

48
00:03:21,792 --> 00:03:23,720
Before increasing praise frequency,

49
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:26,612
check whether the expression matches the
recent action.

50
00:03:26,612 --> 00:03:31,520
Look for moments of accomplishment in the
actual actions of your own game.
